findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading implementation uses unwrap_or_default pattern without distinguishing
    NotFound from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests checking that error messages don't leak internal
    paths/stack traces in exit_codes.rs. However, the reviewer did not flag the actual
    eprintln Display leak. Partial catch via test intent.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CRLF header injection prevention tests in siem_client.rs (lines\
    \ 291-319). Reviewer verified CWE-113 prevention. However, the core issue \u2014\
    \ using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not flagged."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added dependencies with direct version strings. Reviewer noted a toml
    version mismatch (0.8 vs 0.9) but did not flag the broader issue of using direct
    versions instead of workspace = true for the 6 dependencies.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''ConfigFile silently ignores unknown fields
    including token'' and recommended #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] or explicit warning.
    Also flagged has_token_field() as a no-op stub.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [LOW]: 'config_handles_empty_file assertion is vacuous\
    \ \u2014 A || !A is always true. This test can never fail.' at config_loading.rs:85-88."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test using 'let _ = config;'. The
    reviewer found a different vacuous test (exit_code_success_is_zero) but not this
    specific one about default config lacking assert_eq! checks on server() and token().
